From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LuneOS / webOS Ports <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix callback and time struct types rejected by GCC 15

GCC 14 turned -Wincompatible-pointer-types into an error, exposing two
long-standing type mismatches.

timersource.c declared its locals as GTimeVal while the file's own
g_timer_get_current_time() and g_timer_set_expiration() take struct timeval *.
The two happened to share a layout, so this went unnoticed.

init.c passed _CleanupHookListValue() to g_hash_table_foreach(), which wants a
GHFunc taking (key, value, user_data); the function was written as a GFunc
taking only (value, user_data). Called through the hash table it received the
key where it expected the value and freed the wrong pointer, so this was a real
bug rather than only a diagnostic. It has no other caller.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 batteryd/utils/init.c        | 2 +-
 batteryd/utils/timersource.c | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/batteryd/utils/init.c b/batteryd/utils/init.c
index 7ef55e1..c1c44d6 100644
--- a/batteryd/utils/init.c
+++ b/batteryd/utils/init.c
@@ -142,7 +142,7 @@ PrintHookLists(void)
  * Call this at program shutdown to prevent memory leaks.
  */
 static void
-_CleanupHookListValue(gpointer value, gpointer data)
+_CleanupHookListValue(gpointer key, gpointer value, gpointer data)
 {
     GNamedHookList *namedHookList = (GNamedHookList*)value;
     if (namedHookList)
diff --git a/batteryd/utils/timersource.c b/batteryd/utils/timersource.c
index efb0880..b34adba 100644
--- a/batteryd/utils/timersource.c
+++ b/batteryd/utils/timersource.c
@@ -216,7 +216,7 @@ g_timer_source_new_seconds(guint interval_sec)
     source = g_source_new(&g_timer_source_funcs, sizeof(GTimerSource));
     tsource = (GTimerSource*)source;
 
-    GTimeVal now;
+    struct timeval now;
 
     tsource->interval_ms = 1000*interval_sec;
     tsource->granularity = 1000;
@@ -237,7 +237,7 @@ g_timer_source_set_interval_seconds(GTimerSource *tsource, guint interval_sec, g
 void
 g_timer_source_set_interval(GTimerSource *tsource, guint interval_ms, gboolean from_poll)
 {
-    GTimeVal now;
+    struct timeval now;
 
     g_timer_get_current_time(tsource, &now);
 
